## Using the Spike Arrest Policy

The Spike Arrest policy protects against sudden traffic spikes and can be applied to specific methods and paths. It’s less suited for customer-specific limits unless paired with additional logic.

### Example Configuration

```xml
<SpikeArrest name="Spike-Arrest-Per-Method-And-Path">
    <Rate>10ps</Rate> <!-- 10 requests per second -->
    <Condition>(request.verb = "POST" and request.uri.path = "/v2/group1")</Condition>
</SpikeArrest>
```

### Limitation

Spike Arrest applies globally unless segmented with custom attributes or variables.

